In article <PMURPHY.93Sep23131144@orangutan.cv.nrao.edu>, I wrote:

(about an apparent transceiver problem involving a Milan that seemed to
not work and an Allied Telesys CentreCom that did).

Sigh.  I should have read the specsheets on these boxes before posting.
It turns out that the former is just a simple twisted-pair-to-thinwire
*translator*, whereas the latter is a translator *plus* a repeater.  The
Milan box is suited to stretches of thinnet that have at most 10 systems
on them, and the particular segment the Alpha machine was on here had a
lot more than that.

Sorry for the false alarm.
