Wherever you place the font and do the mkfontdir, it must be in your
font path.  Use xset to see and change the fontpath (read the manpage).
I have seen problems with some bdf files that came from VMS.
First of all, make sure you can read the bdf (it's straight ASCII)
and that nothing happened to it when copying.

Check the XLFD name at the top of the file.  Zero's in the PIXEL_SIZE,
POINT_SIZE, or AVERAGE_WIDTH field are reserved to imply a scaleable
font.  If any of these appear as 0 in a bdf file, that's wrong.  See if
you can fix the bdf.

Peter


