The problem has been reported before but I wonder if there are any
other experiences (and maybe solutions). We have a DEC 4000/610, running OSF
1.3 (same problems under version 1.2) and are exporting 5 partitions
via NFS. About every 3 to 6 days the machine 'freezes' (no answer to ping,
login via console stops after entering password) and the only thing
we can do is a halt/reboot. Last time we had about the same behaviour but
the machine stayed alive, only all nfsd daemons showed the 'U' state
with 'ps' (Uninterruptible sleeping process). No NFS traffic was possible
so another halt/reboot... We have 8 nfsd daemons running.

The problem, including core dumps, has been reported to DEC but no results
so far. It has been suggested that 'rmdir' on an exported partition could be
the cause of the problem but I'm not sure. Anyway, it looks like a deadlock
or race condition to me.

Any experiences/suggestions are welcome.

Henk Mos






 
