It would help if you told us which problems you have.
If it is about compiling, this has been discussed in the alpha-osf-managers
mailing list. Basically, what you have to do is the following :
edit lib/config.h. Find the line which defines INTEGER_TYPE to be a long,
and replace 'long' with 'int'.
The comment describes that this type should be a 32-bit integer type.
long is 64 bits an alpha, but int is 32 bits.
Then you just make.
In case you didn't know, you can save time and disk space by skipping
the make trip-trap.
In case you know somebody who has an AIP (alpha Innovator's Program) CD :
Tex should be on it. (I say should because I haven't seen such a CD
myself yet)


