If you *really* need unaligned access to objects that are misaligned
on purpose, you can either write portable code by using byte accesses
and assembling into words or the (faster) way is to use an extension
to C provided by the Alpha/OSF/1 compilers which will generate the
more efficient unaligned access code sequences found in the Alpha
architecture:

main()
{
  char mis[10];
  __unaligned int *p;

  p = (int *) (mis + 1);
  return(*p);
}

