I just did this.  Don't modify scsi_data.c for OSF/1, modify
cam_data.c instead.  Structures are basically the same.
You can use the density tables for the TKZ09 if you like.  That's
really an Exabyte 8500 with a Digital badge on it.  I just copied
the entry labelled "DIGITAL   TKZ09" and replaced the string with
"EXABYTE EXB-8500", 16

Also, make sure you spell "EXABYTE" correctly.  The string compare
functions are too dumb to recognize "EXEBYTE" as the same thing :-)

I was able to write a tape at low density after rebuilding the kernel.
