Setting following parameters should help:

ubcmaxpercent   10
swapbuffers     4

Also using lazy swap allocation policy (aka. removing /sbin/swapdefault) may
help a bit, BUT BE AWARE: lazy swap may cause unexpected process terminations of
processes in the case you run out of swap space (victim may be any process in
system!).

More improvement you get by installing V1.3, and I would recommend it!

And of course, running this on NFS mounted file system locking on may
cause extra overhead, but I suspect this might get better too in V1.3 
because I suspect that compiler makes  less i/o in V1.3.

