First - thanks to the following who responded to my query:

jansen@fosters.astro.wisc.edu
breault@aladdin.mc.ti.com

Most of the following was accomplished prior to the query and small details
were only what was needed.

On the OSF box:

add the qualified hosts in the Security menu of the Session Manager Option
Menu.  The xhost command will allow a quick peek at what's already there.

add the qualified hosts and their remote user-ids to your .rhosts file.

On the VMS box (we run UCX, so this is UCX specific):

UCX> add proxy /host=OSFhost_or_I.P._number/remote_user=OSF_userID VMS_userID

Authorize> add/proxy OSFnode::OSFuserID VMSuserID/default


Then I created a .COM procedure very similar to the one 
jansen@fosters.astro.wisc.edu sent me as a template:

$! DECW_REMOTE.COM
$ if p1 .eqs. "" then p1 = "OSF-HOST.DOMAIN"
$ display = p1
$ set display/create/node='display'/transport=tcpip
$ set process/name="DXterm '' f$getjpi("","PID")'"
$ node = f$trnlnm("sys$node") - ":" - ":"
$ create /terminal=decterm /detached /insert /type_ahead /little_font

Finally, I created an application menu item "DECterm VMS-host"
with a menu command of:

rsh -l VMSuserID VMSnodename '@sys$login:decw_remote.com "OSFhost.domain"' &

and all's well...


Randy
HaymanR@icefog.uacn.alaska.edu


